WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.980
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.770
I hope we have a good time together

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:19.240
Nekogami Yaoyorozu

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:19.240
FFFpeeps presents

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.620
Today let's keep

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.240
Sharing laughs

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:26.670
You take care of my true wishes in secret

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:34.220
You always cheer me up after bad days

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:40.580
I'm sure everyone has known it since childhood

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:49.250
You pretend you don't care, but you're always a good friend

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:58.650
You have another busy day as a god; you just can't help but help out others

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:04.990
Everyone is cheered up by your love

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:13.300
I love always being together while you help others

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:20.820
I'll protect that precious smile; you know what I mean

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.820
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:53.700
All right!

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:58.930
Can you put that strange box away,
at least when you're minding the store?

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:01.100
By "strange box" do you mean this?

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:01.550
Yes.

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:03.620
My, you're not very knowledgeable, are you?

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:07.670
This is the world's first color
handheld game console. It's wonderful!

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.150
Hello!

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.900
Is Yuzu-chan here?

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.490
Oh, Haruka, nice to see you.

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:16.470
As for Yuzu, she should be coming back soon. Just wait a bit.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.280
Mayu-chan, who's that girl next to you?

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.220
U-Um, I'm—

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.450
Her name's Amane. Just someone I know.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:24.860
She's staying here right now.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:27.500
I see. She's your friend, huh?

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.220
Nice to meet you!

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:29.340
No, I'm not really her friend—

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:30.620
Maybe you should prepare some tea for the guest?

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:31.870
Y-Yes, right away!

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:33.040
Yeah, get on it.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:37.830
Your friend looks diligent, unlike you, Mayu-chan.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.010
She's too uptight.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:50.850
That slacker of a cat is making me feel flustered.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.480
I'm still too ashamed to face Kukuri-sama.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.380
The battery level is critically low.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.260
What's this?

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:05.590
Not many good things have happened to me lately, so I thought I'd ask you to drive out the evil spirits.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:07.330
You're a goddess, supposedly.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.700
Drop the "supposedly."

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.770
Let me pray.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:19.720
How's that?

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.720
What was that for, Mayu-chan?

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:29.700
I gave you a miracle forehead flick packed with 500 yen's worth of divine power.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:30.860
Be grateful!

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:33.730
500 yen for a forehead flick? I'm not grateful at all!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.140
Does it drive out evil spirits?

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.350
Oh, yes! It sure does!

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:40.950
I'm back!

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.070
Welcome back, Yuzu-chan.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.490
Oh, Haruka-san, welcome!

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:51.630
All right, I'm off to Granny A and B's cheap candy shop.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.250
Hey, Amane, come with me!

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:54.500
What for?

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:58.170
You thought a game console was a box.
You need some worldly experience.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.630
No, thank you.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.190
Oh, come on.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.680
I'll buy you candy.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:10.380
What's so funny?

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.320
So you do have a childish side.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:13.150
What?

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:15.090
You were easily lured in when I mentioned candy.

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:17.090
Th-That's not true!

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:21.680
In order to show Tsukuyomi-sama what a useless cat you are, I need to observe your daily—

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:22.830
Yeah, yeah.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:27.600
You worry about yourself.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.360
When are you planning on returning to Heaven and talking to Tsukuyomi-sama?

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:36.940
What, Amane? Do you want to talk it over with Tsukuyomi-sama that quickly?

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.610
Th-That's...

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:44.570
Yebisu Store

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.240
Well, it won't go well if we go there alone.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.890
First we need to get as many on our side as we can.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:46.410
On our side?

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:47.510
Get whom on our side?

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:48.850
Don't be so hasty.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.350
Oh, it's Mayu!

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:52.740
Mayu, show us how to do this.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:55.900
What, is that how you ask someone to teach you?

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:00.060
Mayu is a goddess, so you need to ask her more politely.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.220
Got it.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:04.100
How do you defeat this monster?

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.040
You don't get it, do you?

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.280
Oh, this one?

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.400
Let's see. These levels should be enough.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:13.410
Set aside these two to cast magic and raise your defense and attack stats, then attack the monster with the other two.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:18.490
Magic also works on this monster, so you should try to lower the enemy's defense stats.

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:20.380
Now just keep launching direct attacks.

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:20.650
AAAAAAAAA

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:20.650
Defeated Gebon!

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:22.920
You did it!

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:23.890
You're as awesome as ever!

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.690
There you go. Remember to save.

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:27.030
Thank you, goddess!

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.330
This is a small token of thanks.

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:30.410
Oh, I don't need it, but I'll take it.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:31.970
Help us again when we get stuck!

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:33.490
Any time!

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:34.740
What should I do with this?

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:41.290
Here, you can have this.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.640
So stop crying.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:45.540
Okay!

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.760
Sorry she troubled you, Mayu-sama.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.070
She gave me this!

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:50.760
Thank you very much.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:51.910
Please have this.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.420
A persimmon? It looks delicious!

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.760
You can have one too, goddess.

00:05:57.450 --> 00:05:58.960
What's going on?

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:03.360
Yebisu Store

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.910
This is the candy shop.

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:03.630
Let's go inside.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.220
Look, Granny B, we have a customer!

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:08.910
What, Granny A, a customer?

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:11.010
How are you, Granny A, Granny B?

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.820
Oh, it's a goddess.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:16.190
We're doing well. Thank you.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:18.760
Someone gave us persimmons just now. Would you like some?

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:20.110
My, thank you!

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:21.600
Here and here.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:23.150
My, thank you!

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:25.250
We should give them some freebies!

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:26.870
We should give them some for free!

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:28.970
Mayu-sama and the goddess over there!

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:30.870
Please take whatever you'd like.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.660
Oh, thank you!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.330
The "Straw Millionaire" story?

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.600
These are beautiful.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.780
How is it, Amane? Isn't it tasty?

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.490
Is it all right for me to sit here
relaxing and munching on snacks?

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.870
No, it's not! It's not okay!

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:52.170
Am I swayed this easily?

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:55.020
You look dejected.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:57.430
How about you take things a little easier?

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:00.850
No, this is my personal problem.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:04.410
Back there, I got caught up in the moment and...

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:08.020
She's inadequate to be your successor, Kukuri-hime.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:09.160
Amane!

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.320
...abandoned my post.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:13.960
It's hopeless. That was an absolutely unforgivable blunder.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.610
I feel so ashamed that I want to disappear.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:17.710
Hey, pull yourself together, Amane.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:23.050
I plan to convince Tsukuyomi-sama that you'll make a better guardian cat than me, you know?

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:23.950
I can't.

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:28.410
Why? If you messed up once, just apologize. Everything will be fine.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:34.420
I abandoned my post during an unusual surge of Nezumi, in the middle of a critical situation.

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:38.080
Isn't that outbreak of Nezumi just a temporary thing?

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:42.760
It's not like they're infesting Earth with their squeaking—

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:45.500
Yeah, squeaking just like that.

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:52.600
Mayu, step back!

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:56.150
It's nimbler than usual!

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:57.840
You aren't getting away!

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:58.860
Amane!

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:14.040
That Nezumi...

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.860
What happened? Did you get it?

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:17.590
No, it escaped.

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:21.310
It's because I failed to kill it at the first strike!

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:25.620
Amane, it's too early to condemn yourself.

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.850
Thanks for heeding my call!

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:37.680
Are they this town's cats?

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:42.700
Do you think that hunting for Nezumi is the exclusive responsibility of guardian cats?

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:45.280
All species of cats have to chase Nezumi.

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:47.530
Or rather, it's an instinct.

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:53.750
The real hunt begins now!

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:24.180
Sorry, but it's game over.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:27.080
Give up and surrender.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:28.560
It doesn't know when to give up!

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.580
I don't have a grudge against you, nor are you guilty.

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:35.080
However...

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:39.880
I won't let a being from the Underworld ravage Earth!

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:54.380
I think I'll return to the Moon by myself.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:56.390
Oh, why by yourself?

00:09:56.390 --> 00:10:01.410
I should apologize for irresponsibly abandoning my post.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:02.390
Also...

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.110
it seems I misunderstood many things:

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:09.640
about humans and about Nezumi,

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:12.610
and about what's in Tsukuyomi and Kukuri-sama's minds.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:17.510
I've been chasing Nezumi because Tsukoyomi-sama ordered me to,

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:21.780
and I thought Kukuri-sama was of the same mindset,

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:23.950
but I was probably wrong.

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:25.420
I think I understand it now.

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:26.770
I see.

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:29.630
And about you, too.

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:30.680
Me?

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.590
What about me?

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:34.200
That's... well...

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:35.900
What is it?

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:39.530
I think I see why you want to stay here.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:42.820
It would certainly be nice to live in this town, with humans.

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:47.810
Having a cozy time together!

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:51.320
Give my regards and thanks to Yuzu-san.

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:53.250
Tell her that yourself.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:56.180
Um, well, I don't like saying goodbye.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:56.950
I see.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:11:00.870
I should make restitution for my mistakes myself.

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:01.710
Likewise,

00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:05.670
if you're going to take on Tsukuyomi-sama, you're on your own.

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:09.470
You're heartless!

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:15.470
Amane, you've become a fine girl.

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:17.460
That's nice.

00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:22.630
What's going to come out, I wonder?

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:24.120
I can't see anything!

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.400
May I come in?

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:37.830
Welcome, Sasana-san!

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.740
Hello, Kuroe-san!

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:42.190
Madam told me you'd be coming today.

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:44.750
Oh, is that you, Sasana?

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:45.990
Meiko!

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:47.340
Hello!

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:50.420
Why are you at Mayu-sama's family home?

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:52.340
Because I have business here, of course!

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:54.200
I'm sorry to say this,

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:58.920
but Mayu's mother summoned me today to discuss an important matter regarding Mayu-sama.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:01.980
You should come again another day, Meiko-san.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:03.520
What are you talking about?

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:08.980
I was summoned here today. Aren't you the one who got the date wrong?

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:12.360
Of course not! You're the one who's mistaken, no question about it!

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.330
There's no way that I could be mistaken!

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:20.450
Madam summoned both of you.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:26.980
Sasana, Meiko, sorry to call you at such short notice.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:28.710
You two...

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:32.210
seem to be growling at each other even more today.

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:34.770
Madam, please do not let it bother you.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:38.310
Meiko-san is ill-mannered by nature, so please forgive her.

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:41.200
Sasana, you're as insensitive to the situation as always.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.980
I'm amazed by your hopelessly carefree ignorance.

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:51.450
I summoned you two to discuss an important matter.

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:53.710
It's about my daughter, Mayu.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:56.290
Could that matter be...

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:59.040
At first, I thought it was odd because you also called Meiko,

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:05.840
but you're finally going to get rid of this insolent third wheel
who's come between my fiancée Mayu-sama and me, aren't you?

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:10.210
I'd expect no less from Mayu's mother, whom they call the toughest lady of the cat god family!

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:16.310
She must have chosen me, of the house of Daikokuten, over a country girl whose only merit is her humility!

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:19.050
What I wanted to discuss was...

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:19.940
Gulp!

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:24.400
...this unthinkable thing Amaterasu-sama sent us the other day.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:28.320
I wanted to know what Mayu had done to cause this.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.060
Thanks for the food.

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:48.750
Mayu-sama, are you done eating?

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:51.910
Well, yeah, I thought I'd get only eight-tenths full.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:57.420
Um, are things, well, difficult if you're full?

00:13:58.220 --> 00:13:58.820
Is what difficult?

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:00.380
If you're done, I'll take your baked seaweed.

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:06.010
I'm not really sure, but maybe you can't rise to Heaven easily if your body feels heavy.

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:10.320
Or perhaps your belly gets stuck if it's too big.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.650
Gets stuck on what exactly?

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:13.160
That's an interesting theory, Yuzu.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.270
Huh? Am I wrong?

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:20.240
Well, I'll be seeing Tsukuyomi-sama, so I don't want to eat too much and feel sluggish.

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:23.040
That's an unusually admirable thing for you to say.

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:24.750
Oh, Gonta, when did you get here?

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.550
I've been here the whole time!

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:29.180
I didn't notice because your presence was so weak.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.950
Shut up! More importantly...

00:14:32.390 --> 00:14:34.990
Mayu, leave Yuzu-san to me!

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:35.790
What?

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:39.680
I'll make sure Yuzu-san doesn't feel lonely even when you're gone!

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:41.380
That's great.

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:44.830
What's more, the business will have
a better chance of thriving if I'm here.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:48.800
You just play games all day, but I'll work very hard.

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:51.200
Well, I'm certainly visiting Heaven,

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:54.120
but I'm just stopping by there on my way to the Moon.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:52.890
She's not listening!

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:55.780
I don't plan to return home,

00:14:55.780 --> 00:14:59.410
so I'll be back right after I'm done
talking things over with Tsukuyomi-sama.

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:00.270
I see.

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:01.100
All right.

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:09.950
I'll be going, then.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:17.440
See you.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:24.890
She's gone.

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:39.220
All right, it looks like I got to Takamagahara safely.

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:42.400
However, Takamagahara is now enemy territory.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:46.890
Although Mother did un-disown me,
she's clearly plotting something.

00:15:46.890 --> 00:15:50.390
I need to hurry to Tsukuyomi-sama's mansion before they notice my presence.

00:15:50.390 --> 00:15:53.600
Oh, isn't it you, Mayu-sama?

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.500
Someone found me already!

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:57.750
When did you return to Heaven?

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:00.700
Oh, it's you, Kuroe. Don't surprise me like that.

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:04.760
It's been a while, so why don't we gather some folks and play mahjong or hanafuda?

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:06.260
As much as I'd love to...

00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:10.790
I'm just here today to meet Tsukuyomi-sama in secret.

00:16:10.790 --> 00:16:12.980
I can't go back home for a certain reason.

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:15.130
I see. You're making a secret visit.

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:19.600
Then let me give you a big helping hand!

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:24.330
Let me open a road to the interior of Tsukuyomi-sama's mansion for you!

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:29.040
Now, Mayu-sama! Hurry and go!

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:31.290
You've become better at spells, haven't you?

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:32.890
I owe you one, Kuroe!

00:16:34.290 --> 00:16:35.210
Huh?

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:37.250
This place is...

00:16:39.300 --> 00:16:41.800
Hey, Kuroe, what's the meaning of this?

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:45.690
This is the confinement cell of my house, no matter how I look at it!

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:48.030
Mayu-sama, forgive me.

00:16:48.030 --> 00:16:50.550
Before I can be your friend,

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:54.560
I have to be a loyal retainer to the head cat god family.

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:12.050
This is strange.

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:16.170
I was looking forward to having a meal alone with Yuzu-san like this,

00:17:16.170 --> 00:17:18.530
but what's this tension in the air?

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:21.210
I feel like I'm starting to suffocate.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:28.870
Yuzu-san's a delicate beauty,

00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:32.350
but she'd look even lovelier if she smiled.

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:37.690
All right, I'll tell my funniest and
wittiest story and make Yuzu-san smile!

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:39.120
Y-Yuzu-than!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:39.640
Huh?

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:41.030
I fumbled already!

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.380
I-I mean, Yuzu-san!

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:45.520
So I was riding the bus the other day.

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:46.300
Yes?

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:49.150
And an old man who was getting off the bus before me—

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:50.750
This story won't work!

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:53.450
I can't say he farted and got off the bus.

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:55.000
We're eating a meal!

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:58.460
Yuzu-san will despise me if I tell that kind of story.

00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:59.100
Gonta-san, you're a horrible man!

00:17:59.100 --> 00:17:59.580
Probably forever.

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:01.120
Gonta-san?

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:02.950
What did the old man getting off the bus do?

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:05.020
Actually, forget about the old man.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:08.090
So I was riding the bus that day.

00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:14.230
Maybe because it was so late at night, but aside from me, only a man in a pretentious suit was on board.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.920
A pretentious suit?

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:17.930
Yes, it was clearly pretentious.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:21.400
That bus had seats facing the sides,

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:23.510
and the man in the suit was sitting there.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:25.570
I was sitting in the very back.

00:18:25.570 --> 00:18:29.390
Then the man in the pretentious suit struck a cool pose.

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:32.100
So that was the cool pose, huh?

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:36.340
Good, the story is working well. This is the right mood!

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:41.930
Maybe because it was so late at night, but the bus went smoothly, skipping empty bus stops.

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:42.950
Then suddenly...

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:46.280
I got the latest game console from Yukina!

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:47.520
Shamo-chan!

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:49.040
Huh? Isn't Mayu here?

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:51.290
She's out right now.

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:53.390
Then I'll come back later.

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:55.370
I'll leave this here.

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:56.540
Bye!

00:18:57.730 --> 00:18:59.440
That scared me.

00:18:59.440 --> 00:19:02.790
I was so close to the punchline! Jeez, Shamo-san!

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:05.600
Yuzu-san, do you remember the story I was just telling you?

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:08.440
The bus was going smoothly when suddenly—

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:11.430
Mayu-sama asked me for a favor, but I couldn't!

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:16.050
She asked me to take care of Yaoyorozu-dou while she's away,

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:19.230
but I really had to help out my grandpa today, so I apologize.

00:19:19.230 --> 00:19:20.820
I'll come again tomorrow!

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:22.640
See you!

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:26.300
Well, Yuzu-san, so the bus was—

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:27.060
Gonta-san!

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:27.570
Yes?

00:19:27.570 --> 00:19:32.080
Why don't you save that story for later
and help yourself to some food?

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:34.110
Yes, let's do that.

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:40.030
My plan to make Yuzu-san smile with
my funny and witty story has failed.

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:42.720
Well, it's not a very funny story anyway.

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:47.180
But Yuzu-san is smiling, so I guess it all worked out?

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:48.600
All right! Time to eat!

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:56.020
Gonta-san, that's amazing!

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:57.680
Is it delicious?

00:19:57.680 --> 00:19:58.850
Yes, it is!

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:00.610
Bad news! Bad news!

00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:01.600
Mayu will be attending...

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:03.070
...a meeting for an arranged marriage!

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:04.600
What?

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:05.700
With whom?

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:07.470
Tsukuyomi-sama!

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:11.530
He's second in Heaven, just below Amaterasu-sama!

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:15.160
How did that happen?

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:17.710
Isn't that completely different from what Amane-san said?

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:22.480
She was talking about Mayu becoming Kukuri-hime's guardian cat in Amane's place, right?

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:23.960
How did that become a marriage meeting?

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:27.720
Exactly! And I'm Mayu's fiancé!

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:31.750
Putting that aside, we don't know how it came about either!

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.520
But there's no way Mayu would agree to it!

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:38.730
If someone of such high rank is asking, won't refusing be difficult?

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:47.240
Mayu-sama won't be coming back anymore?

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:53.740
Kuroe.

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:58.810
I won't run away, so can you let me out for just a little while?

00:20:58.810 --> 00:21:00.990
How about we play a little game?

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:02.770
You really won't run away?

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:04.490
No, I won't!

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:07.690
Look! Right here!

00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:10.140
Dice to play chinchirorin!

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:12.910
Trying to tempt me won't work.

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:16.140
I've become more serious since then!

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:19.070
Tsk, that's no fun.

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:20.890
This is a problem.

00:21:20.890 --> 00:21:23.190
What should I do?

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:29.150
D-Don't tell me...

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:36.040
Mayu, you got captured sooner than I expected.

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:37.910
Mother!

00:21:37.910 --> 00:21:42.920
I have many, many things I need to ask you.

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:49.420
So prepare yourself!

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:09.190
I gently peered into the future which we call tomorrow

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:13.320
Looking at the world upside down

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:20.360
I projected my memories upon the glittering cotton candy clouds

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:24.490
And hung rainbow ribbons

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:31.790
When I'm left alone, I feel lonely and depressed

00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:38.260
So stay here forever

00:22:38.260 --> 00:22:43.510
I'm sure everyone has some

00:22:43.510 --> 00:22:49.430
Unfulfilled desires locked inside their hearts

00:22:51.690 --> 00:23:01.610
I want you to realize that small memory that won't disappear is the key. Yeah

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:08.080
You're always the only one

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:12.370
Who can make me reminisce fondly

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:41.370
Next Episode

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:31.120
I think I heard Mayu-sama's voice just now!

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:33.150
If we don't go, who will?

00:23:33.150 --> 00:23:33.750
Of course I'll go!

00:23:33.750 --> 00:23:35.670
I packed some food.

00:23:35.670 --> 00:23:37.870
Yuzu-san's homemade meals!

00:23:38.340 --> 00:23:39.950
Let's go, Gonta!

00:23:39.950 --> 00:23:41.300
What, me too?
